WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.210
Hi! After reading a short story, we answer questions. Some answers are in the text, and some need thinking. Today we'll learn reading comprehension.

2
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.450
Sam's kite got stuck in a tall tree.

3
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.282
He frowned and kicked a stone.

4
00:00:18.432 --> 00:00:21.906
His sister fetched a long pole from the shed.

5
00:00:22.056 --> 00:00:26.970
Soon the kite was flying again, and Sam grinned.

6
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:33.546
The first kind: the answer is in the text. Find the sentence: where did the kite get stuck?

7
00:00:33.696 --> 00:00:39.570
The second kind uses clues: frowning and kicking a stone show Sam was upset.

8
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.178
Answer in full sentences, and answer exactly what is asked.

9
00:00:44.328 --> 00:00:48.642
After writing, check back in the text.

10
00:00:48.792 --> 00:00:53.466
Watch out! The question asks about the end, not the start!

11
00:00:53.616 --> 00:00:57.978
At the end the kite flew again and Sam grinned, so he was happy.

12
00:00:58.128 --> 00:01:03.090
Add a reason with because to make the answer complete.

13
00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:11.034
Your turn! Where did the kite get stuck? Pause and think.

14
00:01:11.184 --> 00:01:17.130
The text says it got stuck in a tall tree. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:26.178
Another one! Which word shows Sam was upset at first? Pause and think.

16
00:01:26.328 --> 00:01:32.562
Frowned means his face showed he was unhappy. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:32.712 --> 00:01:40.194
Here's another! Who helped Sam? Pause and think.

18
00:01:40.344 --> 00:01:46.794
His sister helped him; she fetched a long pole. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:46.944 --> 00:01:54.978
Try one more! Where did the pole come from? Pause and think.

20
00:01:55.128 --> 00:02:00.282
The text says from the shed. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:00.432 --> 00:02:08.106
Try one more! What does grinned mean? Pause and think.

22
00:02:08.256 --> 00:02:15.738
The kite flew again and he was happy, so grinned means smiled widely. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:15.888 --> 00:02:23.730
Try one more! Why did Sam frown? Pause and think.

24
00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:29.706
Because his kite was stuck in a tall tree. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:29.856 --> 00:02:37.818
Last one! How did Sam feel at the end? Pause and think.

26
00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:44.466
His kite flew again and he grinned, so he was happy. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:44.616 --> 00:02:56.082
Remember: read the story, then read the question carefully. Some answers are found in the text; others need clues. Answer in full sentences, and check back at the end.

28
00:02:56.232 --> 00:03:02.441
Read a short story today and say how the main character feels, and why!

